details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two simple, matte ceramic soup bowls placed on an aged oak wood surface with visible grain and slight use marks. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, ensuring the bowls are fully visible and perfectly framed. A shallow depth of field keeps the front bowl sharp while the second bowl behind it is softly blurred. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the velvety sheen of the soup. The soup is a vibrant, smooth, opaque sunset-orange color, thick and uniform. In the center of each bowl sits a deliberate, slightly imperfect swirl of white Greek yogurt, topped with a rustic scattering of dark green, roasted pumpkin seeds that provide a crunchy texture. Props include a tarnished silver soup spoon resting casually on the wood near the foreground bowl and a small, rumpled linen napkin placed off-center. A few stray pumpkin seeds are scattered naturally on the tabletop near a small, half-full ceramic ramekin of additional seeds in the background. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: a tiny splash of soup on the rim of the bowl, an asymmetric yogurt dollop, uneven seed distribution. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a small smudge of spice on the table. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature—cozy and inviting, not cold or clinical. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
